00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:51,000
A '60s radical. An uptight fed. It's gonna be a real trip!

2
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:36,000
Flashback is a action, comedy, crime film directed by Franco Amurri.

3
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:21,000
A hippie radical, Huey Walker has been a fugitive for decades,
accused of a crime that he may not have committed.

4
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:06,000
Finally apprehended, Walker is escorted to trial by
uptight 20-something FBI agent John Buckner.

5
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:51,000
While the two seem to be polar opposites, it turns out that Buckner may have more in common with Walker than is
initially apparent, a point that is driven home when the pair faces off against a sinister small-town sheriff.

6
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:36,000
Huey Walker, played by Dennis Hopper.

7
00:47:15,000 --> 00:47:21,000
John Buckner, played by Kiefer Sutherland.

8
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Maggie, played by Carol Kane.

9
01:00:45,000 --> 01:00:51,000
Stark, played by Paul Dooley.

10
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
Sheriff Rand Hightower, played by Cliff DeYoung.

11
01:14:15,000 --> 01:14:21,000
Barry, played by Richard Masur.

12
01:21:00,000 --> 01:21:06,000
Flashback is a 1990 American adventure comedy film starring
Dennis Hopper, Kiefer Sutherland, and Carol Kane.

13
01:27:45,000 --> 01:27:51,000
The film is written by David Loughery and directed by Franco Amurri.

14
01:34:30,000 --> 01:34:36,000
The film explores themes of hippie, yuppie, fbi, lsd, fake identity.

15
01:41:15,000 --> 01:41:21,000
